DevOps Interview Preparation – Tool 10

GCP Cloud (Basics + Advanced) | 0–2 Years Experience

GCP is widely used for cloud-native, Kubernetes, and data-driven platforms.
Interviewers check whether you understand core GCP services + how GCP is used in DevOps pipelines.

Focus: GCP Interview Questions (Basics + Advanced)

• What is Google Cloud Platform (GCP)?
• GCP global infrastructure (Regions, Zones)
• What is a GCP project? Why is it important?
• What is Compute Engine?
• Difference between Compute Engine and AWS EC2
• What are machine types in GCP?
• What is an image and snapshot in GCP?
• What is Google Cloud Storage (GCS)?
• GCS storage classes
• What is Identity and Access Management (IAM) in GCP?
• Role types in GCP (Primitive, Predefined, Custom)
• What is a service account?
• Difference between user account and service account
• What is VPC in GCP?
• Difference between default and custom VPC
• What is a subnet in GCP?
• Firewall rules in GCP
• What is Cloud Load Balancing?
🔹 Advanced GCP Concepts (Beginner-Friendly)

• What is Google Kubernetes Engine (GKE)?
• Difference between GKE and self-managed Kubernetes
• What is Cloud Run?
• Cloud Run vs GKE
• What is Cloud Functions?
• When do you use Cloud Functions?
• What is Cloud Build?
• Cloud Build vs Jenkins
• What is Artifact Registry?
• Container Registry vs Artifact Registry
• What is Stackdriver (Cloud Operations)?
• Logging vs Monitoring in GCP
• What is Cloud Pub/Sub (basic idea)?
• What is Terraform role in GCP?
• How do you secure workloads in GCP?
• Common GCP mistakes freshers make
• Real-world GCP DevOps use case

Interview Tip:
If you can explain:
👉 “Code → Build → Container → GKE → Monitor on GCP”
you already sound like a cloud-native DevOps engineer, even with 0–2 years of experience.
